<?xml version="1.0" encoding="windows-1251"?>
<!--
  Context Menu Overhaul — Anthology 2.1 adaptation, safety-net fix.

  mod_menu_anthology_2_1.ltx references the label id "st_seqload_menu" for the
  Mags Redux sequential-loading submenu (used in [label_icons]/[groups]/[chevrons]
  to attach an icon and chevron to that row). That id is only ever used as a
  LOOKUP KEY there — it does not define the on-screen text. If R.A.K Mags Redux
  does not itself ship a translation for exactly this id, the engine has
  nothing to render and falls back to printing the raw string id
  ("st_seqload_menu") as the row's label.

  This file defines that string as a fallback. Prefix "2_" makes it load after
  Mags Redux's own text files (alphabetically after "0_"/"1_"-prefixed base
  files most packs use) so if Mags Redux already defines "st_seqload_menu"
  correctly, that definition is simply overwritten by an identical-intent
  string here — harmless either way.

  If the row still shows raw text in game after installing this, Mags Redux is
  using a DIFFERENT id for that row (typo/rename on its side) — check its own
  text xml for the real id and update [label_icons]/[groups]/[chevrons] in
  mod_menu_anthology_2_1.ltx to match it instead.
-->
<string_table>
    <string id="st_seqload_menu">
        <text>Sequential loading</text>
    </string>
</string_table>
